[
    {
        "content": "<p>I just had CI fail on a push that included the following bit of text, because the style linter complained:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>We set up the endomorphism of `ℙ²` that on affine points with affine sum is equal to\n```\n(x(P) * x(Q) : x(P) + x(Q) : 1) ↦ (x(P+Q) * x(P-Q) : x(P+Q) + x(P-Q) : 1) ;\n```\nsee `WeierstrassCurve.addSubMap` (this is on coordinate vectors).\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>What did the linter complain about?</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>error: ...xxx.lean:3: This line contains a space before a semicolon\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>\n<p>Complaining about text within code blocks within docstrings seems to me a bit over-aggressive...</p>",
        "id": 601867188,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1781112644
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't understand though what the meaning of the semicolon is.</p>",
        "id": 601899958,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781119500
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's punctuation before the \"see ...\". The space in front of it was intended to improve readability.</p>",
        "id": 601900205,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1781119558
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Punctuation should not be in a code block, in my opinion.</p>",
        "id": 601901233,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781119793
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>How would you write it then? (Math journals usually insist on punctuation at the end of displayed equations when grammar asks for it.) Would using LaTeX be better?</p>",
        "id": 601901838,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1781119934
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suppose I would not use punctuation here, and capitalize the next line <span aria-label=\"shrug\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f937\" role=\"img\" title=\"shrug\">:shrug:</span></p>",
        "id": 601908848,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781121558
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the difference with a formula in latex is that a code block is really a clear visual block/quotation that marks the inside as code. If you really wanted, you could write it like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">We</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">up</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">endomorphism</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`ℙ</span><span class=\"bp\">²`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">that</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">affine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">points</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">affine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">equal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">`;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">see</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`WeierstrassCurve.addSubMap</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coordinate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vectors</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 601909899,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781121801
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479359\">Michael Stoll</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Style.20linter.20too.20picky.3F/near/601901838\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would using LaTeX be better?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I would say yes; code blocks only make sense for things which are actually valid lean code, which this is not</p>",
        "id": 601952130,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781133406
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479299\">Jovan Gerbscheid</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Style.20linter.20too.20picky.3F/near/601909899\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think the difference with a formula in latex is that a code block is really a clear visual block/quotation that marks the inside as code. If you really wanted, you could write it like this:</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">We</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">up</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">endomorphism</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`ℙ</span><span class=\"bp\">²`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">that</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">affine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">points</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">affine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">equal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">`;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">see</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`WeierstrassCurve.addSubMap</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coordinate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vectors</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I wanted to format this bit as separate line (like a displayed equation), which this version does not do.</p>",
        "id": 602054045,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1781164003
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Style.20linter.20too.20picky.3F/near/601952130\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479359\">Michael Stoll</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Style.20linter.20too.20picky.3F/near/601901838\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would using LaTeX be better?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I would say yes; code blocks only make sense for things which are actually valid lean code, which this is not</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Does the linter skip LaTeX-formatted text? (I guess I'll just try it out and come back to complain again if it deosn't...)</p>",
