    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479359\">Michael Stoll</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Style.20linter.20too.20picky.3F/near/602054045\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479299\">Jovan Gerbscheid</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Style.20linter.20too.20picky.3F/near/601909899\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think the difference with a formula in latex is that a code block is really a clear visual block/quotation that marks the inside as code. If you really wanted, you could write it like this:</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">We</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">up</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">endomorphism</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`ℙ</span><span class=\"bp\">²`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">that</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">affine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">points</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">affine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">equal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">`;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">see</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`WeierstrassCurve.addSubMap</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coordinate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vectors</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I wanted to format this bit as separate line (like a displayed equation), which this version does not do.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Try this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>We set up the endomorphism of `ℙ²` that on affine points with affine sum is equal to\n\n`(x(P) * x(Q) : x(P) + x(Q) : 1) ↦ (x(P+Q) * x(P-Q) : x(P+Q) + x(P-Q) : 1)`;\n\nsee `WeierstrassCurve.addSubMap` (this is on coordinate vectors).\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Unfortunately, markdown does not natively support center align text.</p>",
        "id": 602059875,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1781165180
