    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Style.20linter.20too.20picky.3F/near/601952130\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479359\">Michael Stoll</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Style.20linter.20too.20picky.3F/near/601901838\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would using LaTeX be better?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I would say yes; code blocks only make sense for things which are actually valid lean code, which this is not</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>code blocks make sense for many things; in particular since markup allows you to refine the way things are displayed. taking a page from zulips' book, one could add <code>math</code> after the triple backticks to make it sensible.</p>",
